<PageTitle>Data and reuse — StageFold</PageTitle>
<article class="page narrow"><h1>Your film and its copies.</h1><p>The local studio stores a valid scene in this browser only when you Apply. Theme preference also stays in browser storage. JSON, PNG, WebM and offline HTML exports are generated locally. StageFold does not receive uploaded photos, voice or video; this release uses its original vector vocabulary.</p><section><h2>Private shared work</h2><p>Creating or saving a shared film sends its scene JSON to this service's database. The owner, invited editors and viewers can read the current film. Owners and editors can inspect saved revisions; viewers cannot inspect history. All invited readers can keep exported copies. Removing access stops future reads and writes, not a copy already downloaded.</p><p>Accounts use a recovery key and a secure session cookie. Keys and invitations are stored as hashes. There is no email reset or verified-person label. Do not put a recovery key, invitation, personal address or confidential material in a film's captions. Technical logs omit document bodies, credentials and raw network addresses; action limits store salted identifiers.</p></section><section><h2>Public cuts and remixes</h2><p>Publishing sends the saved film, your public alias and its source attribution to the public cutting room under CC BY 4.0. Private member lists, invitations and project history are excluded. The cut is immutable. A later private edit does not update it. Withdrawal stops public serving and new forks while retaining the snapshot for attribution and operator review; existing licensed remixes and exported copies remain.</p><p>Use the Fork action for a source-pinned remix. Exported JSON holds scene data, so you must retain the credit yourself when using it outside this service. Offline HTML films from a public cut include a publisher/source credit.</p></section><section><h2>Reports, accounts and billing</h2><p>Report spam, unsafe content, rights issues or personal information from the cut page. Reports go to the operator queue; the service does not invent an automatic moderation decision. Account deletion removes owned private work and sessions, withdraws published cuts and removes their personal alias. An active paid period must end before account deletion.</p><p>No advertising or third-party analytics runs in the studio. Optional membership checkout remains unavailable unless the merchant key, fixed price and signed webhook are all configured. A checkout return alone never grants membership.</p></section></article>
